    return's own evaluation. Its H7 control is recorded: forcing ruleAsLabel to
    1 makes a run refuse with `REFUSED DO -- parseRule: the generated body
    returned a RULE where a label was owed`, so the guard is reachable and names
    its subject.

    NOT IN -- the close itself. The dispatch asks every generated body to close
    with "the same leaveRule spelling", and ON THIS ROAD THAT SPELLING DOES NOT
    EXIST. leaveRule is a five-argument tok extern (RuleStuff.twk) used inside
    genParse's EMITTED TOK SOURCE, which is built by the compiler. This road
    emits KANT, compiled at run time by compile()/processCode, and a kant action
    takes ONE argument, so leaveRule is not callable from it and is registered
    in no registry. Nor are null, labelNO, trueResult or falseResult, so a kant
    body cannot even spell "return nothing".

